  message: "Stale/already-fixed. Filed claim (2026-06-07): io-boundaries suppresses surviving open/read/write/close into external_potential via python.yaml ambiguous_names. Re-ran the item's own repro on merged dev (.venv/bin/hypergumbo): a 'with open(p) as f: f.read()' module -> io-boundaries reports 'I/O Boundary Map (1 boundary calls) / fs_read: 1 / file.read' with dst python:file:0-0:read:unresolved (module=file), NOT suppressed into external_potential (external_potential bucket absent). Fixed by WI-fuvuj (e9be75116b, 2026-06-27): receiver-type inference + synthetic 'file' catalog module so open()-idiom .read()/.write() classify via lookup_with_module, not ambiguous_names suppression. Residual breadth (file.close, immediate-chain .write) tracked distinctly by WI-higaj; not re-opened here."  # 0ade
